---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StoreButtons from '../components/StoreButtons.astro';

// How Hot Mess is positioned (Rick, 2026-11-14): no targeted ads and no ad tracking. Venues and events that would
// show up in Hot Mess anyway can sponsor premium placement, always disclosed as "Sponsored". Outside brands can't buy
// ads. Publisher (Soapbox) stories carry the publisher's own ad relationship, kept distinct from Hot Mess's. Keep this page in step with what the apps actually show.
const youSee = [
  {
    title: 'Sponsored venues and events',
    body: 'A venue or an event that’s already in Hot Mess can pay to be shown more prominently. It’s always labelled “Sponsored” and says who paid. Which sponsors you see depends on the place you’re looking at, never on who you are.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Hot Mess announcements',
    body: 'News about Hot Mess itself, like a new feature or a change to the rules. Labelled “Announcement”.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Free cards for queer charities',
    body: 'Community groups and charities we choose to feature, free of charge. Labelled “Charity”.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Our own apps for the people who make the night',
    body: 'Cards about AudienceKit, the platform Hot Mess runs on, and its apps for the people who keep listings up to date: Velvet for venue staff and Backstage for performers and promoters. Labelled “From AudienceKit”. An app’s card hides once you have the app.',
  },
];

const neverDo = [
  'Target ads or sponsored spots at you by who you are, what you look like, who you’re into or where you’ve been.',
  'Let outside brands buy ads, banners or campaigns. Only venues and events already in Hot Mess can sponsor.',
  'Hide that something is paid for. A sponsored spot is always labelled.',
  'Track you for ads: the apps don’t collect your advertising ID or send events to Facebook or any ad network.',
  'Sell or share your data with advertisers or data brokers.',
  'Charge you to use Hot Mess.',
];
---
<Base title="How Hot Mess is paid for" description="Hot Mess is free, with no targeted ads and no ad tracking. Venues and events can sponsor a better spot, always labelled.">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">How Hot Mess is paid for</p>
        <h1>No targeted ads. No tracking.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Hot Mess is free. Nothing in it is aimed at you because of who you are, and nothing follows you around for advertisers. Venues and events that are in Hot Mess anyway can pay for a better spot, and when they do it says “Sponsored”.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="see">
      <h2 id="see">What you might see between listings</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        {youSee.map((r) => (
          <article class="card item">
            <h3>{r.title}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{r.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="muted">None of these are chosen using anything about you: not your profile, your tribes or where you have been. They depend only on the place you’re looking at.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="publishers">
      <h2 id="publishers">News from local publishers</h2>
      <p>Hot Mess can show stories from local queer publishers, like the news for your city. Those stories belong to the publisher, and so does any advertising that comes with them. When you open one, you’re reading the publisher’s own work: they choose and answer for their ads, not Hot Mess. We keep it that way on purpose: those ads help local publishers stay in business and keep paying the writers who cover our community. Hot Mess takes no cut of a publisher’s ad money, just as it takes no cut of the tips you give performers. Hot Mess never shares anything about you with a publisher’s advertisers.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap split" aria-labelledby="never">
      <div>
        <h2 id="never">What we never do</h2>
        <ul>{neverDo.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="different">Why it works this way</h2>
        <p>A lot of free apps are paid for by learning about the people who use them and selling chances to reach them. For a community where being found by the wrong person can mean harassment or being outed, that's the wrong trade.</p>
        <p>We do watch for crashes and slow screens (New Relic) and count visits to this website (Google Analytics), so we can fix things. None of it is used for ads or shared with advertisers.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="where">
      <article class="card where">
        <h2 id="where">Who pays for it</h2>
        <p>Hot Mess is run by <a href="https://lovewins.media">Love Wins Media</a>, which builds <a href="https://audiencekit.com">AudienceKit</a>, the platform Hot Mess runs on. Sponsorships help, and Love Wins Media covers the rest of the hosting, moderation and development.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap get">
      <h2>Get Hot Mess</h2>
      <p class="muted">See also <a href="/safety">Safety</a>, our <a href="https://audiencekit.com/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://audiencekit.com/terms/">Terms</a>.</p>
      <StoreButtons />
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6rem) 0 clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); background: radial-gradient(120% 90% at 10% 0%, var(--accent-soft), transparent 60%); }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; font-size: .85rem; margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6.5vw, 4rem); font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 16ch; }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 52ch; margin: 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 3rem 0 1rem; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .why-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 0 2rem; }
  .why-grid p { margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 60ch; }
  .item { padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem .5rem; }
  .item h3 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 0 2rem; }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  li { margin: .5rem 0; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .75rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; }
  td { font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  tbody th span { display: block; font-weight: 400; font-size: .9rem; }
  .discounts { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .where { margin-top: 3rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent-soft), var(--surface-raised) 70%); }
  .where h2 { margin: 0 0 .75rem; font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .where p { margin: 0; }
  .get h2 { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .get p { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
</style>
